      <title>How Iran war could create a ‘fertiliser shock’ — an often ignored global risk to food prices and farming</title>
      <link>https://www.downtoearth.org.in/agriculture/how-iran-war-could-create-a-fertiliser-shock-an-often-ignored-global-risk-to-food-prices-and-farming</link>
      <description>The closure of the Strait of Hormuz by Iran could trigger a global fertiliser shock, disrupting nitrogen fertiliser transport and impacting food security. This could lead to soaring prices, reduced crop yields, and increased food insecurity, highlighting the fragility of the global food system.</description>
